# Linux-bound and source files must always use LF line endings, even when the
# repo is cloned/checked out on Windows. This prevents the classic
# "$'\r': command not found" crash when shell scripts are copied to a Pi,
# and keeps platform.py / systemd units clean on the target machine.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf
*.md      text eol=lf
*.txt     text eol=lf
